<h3>7.3 Step 1 — add the BLE package</h3>
<p>Open <code>pubspec.yaml</code> and add two lines under <code>dependencies:</code>. Keep the existing
indentation (two spaces).</p>

<pre>dependencies:
  flutter:
    sdk: flutter
  provider: ^6.1.1
  shared_preferences: ^2.2.2
  intl: ^0.19.0
  flutter_blue_plus: ^1.32.12      <span class="c"># ← ADD: Bluetooth Low Energy</span>
  permission_handler: ^11.3.1      <span class="c"># ← ADD: runtime permission prompts</span></pre>

<p>Then, in a terminal at the project root:</p>
<pre>cd /d/sih_test_app_new
flutter pub get</pre>

<div class="warn"><span class="t">You must fully restart, not hot-reload</span>
<p><code>flutter_blue_plus</code> contains native Android code. Hot reload cannot load native plugins.
Stop the app entirely and run <code>flutter run -d &lt;your-phone&gt;</code> again, otherwise you get
