<h1>PRANA &middot; Complete ESP32 &amp; Hardware Integration Guide</h1>
<p style="color: #64748B; font-size: 9pt; margin-bottom: 14pt;">
  Step-by-step developer manual for connecting custom ESP32/nRF/Arduino hardware sensors to the PRANA Flutter App.
</p>

<div class="box">
  <div class="box-title">Summary for Beginners</div>
  You do not need to rewrite the app to connect real hardware. The app already contains a full Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) engine. You only need to configure <strong>three core files</strong> in Flutter and flash the provided <strong>C++ firmware</strong> onto your ESP32.
</div>

<h2>1. The End-to-End Hardware Data Pipeline</h2>

<div class="diag">
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 1. HARDWARE SENSORS (ESP32 Wearable)                                    │
│    MAX30102 (HR/SpO2) + MPU6050 (IMU) + DHT11 (Temp/Humidity)           │
│    Microcontroller packs data into JSON and sends via BLE Notify       │
└───────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘
                                    │ BLE GATT Notify (UUID: beb5483e...)
                                    ▼
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 2. BLE LISTENER: lib/features/devices/bluetooth_sensor_data_source.dart │
│    Discovers PRANA_BAND_PRO, connects, requests 256-byte MTU, listens  │
└───────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘
                                    │ Raw UTF-8 Bytes
                                    ▼
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 3. SENSOR PARSER: lib/features/devices/sensor_parser.dart               │
│    Decodes JSON string into HealthReading, MotionReading, EnvReading   │
└───────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘
                                    │ Emits on broadcast Streams
                                    ▼
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 4. CONTROLLER: lib/core/services/prana_health_controller.dart          │
│    Updates live UI metrics, updates historical charts, triggers AI     │
└───────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘
                                    │ State Notification
                                    ▼
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 5. USER INTERFACE (Dashboard, Health, Risk, Emergency Alerting)        │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
</div>

<h2>2. Exactly Where to Make Changes in the Code</h2>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>File Path</th>
      <th>Section / What to Change</th>
      <th>Why You Change It</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><code>lib/core/constants/ble_constants.dart</code></td>
      <td><code>targetDeviceName</code>, <code>serviceUuid</code>, <code>telemetryStreamCharacteristicUuid</code></td>
      <td>Matches the BLE Name and UUIDs advertised by your ESP32 board.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>lib/features/devices/sensor_parser.dart</code></td>
      <td><code>parseJsonTelemetry()</code>, <code>toHealthReading()</code></td>
      <td>Add or modify custom sensor fields sent from hardware.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>lib/shared/models/health_reading.dart</code></td>
      <td>Class fields &amp; <code>fromJson()</code></td>
      <td>Add new health parameters (e.g. ECG, GSR Stress, Blood Pressure).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>lib/core/services/prana_health_controller.dart</code></td>
      <td><code>_onHealthReadingReceived()</code></td>
      <td>Directs incoming sensor metrics to UI variables and charts.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml</code></td>
      <td>Bluetooth &amp; Location Permissions</td>
      <td>Allows Android to discover and connect to BLE devices (already configured).</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2 class="pb">3. Code Walkthrough: File by File</h2>

<h3>Step 3.1 &mdash; Configure Device Name &amp; UUIDs</h3>
<p>Open <code>lib/core/constants/ble_constants.dart</code>:</p>
<pre><code>class BleConstants {
  BleConstants._();

  // Change this to whatever name you programmed on your ESP32
  static const String targetDeviceName = 'PRANA_BAND_PRO';
  static const String fallbackDevicePrefix = 'PRANA_';

  // Primary Health Service UUID
  static const String serviceUuid = '4fafc201-1fb5-459e-8fcc-c5c9c331914b';

  // JSON Telemetry Stream Characteristic UUID
  static const String telemetryStreamCharacteristicUuid = 'beb5483e-36e1-4688-b7f5-ea07361b26a8';

  // Scan and connect timeouts
  static const int scanTimeoutSeconds = 12;
  static const int connectionTimeoutSeconds = 10;
}</code></pre>

<h3>Step 3.2 &mdash; Parse JSON Sensor Payloads</h3>
<p>Open <code>lib/features/devices/sensor_parser.dart</code>:</p>
<pre><code>// The app accepts structured JSON packets sent from ESP32:
static Map&lt;String, dynamic&gt;? parseJsonTelemetry(String rawString) {
  try {
    final decoded = jsonDecode(rawString) as Map&lt;String, dynamic&gt;;
    return decoded;
  } catch (_) {
    return null; // Gracefully handles corrupted frames
  }
}</code></pre>

<h3>Step 3.3 &mdash; Switch Between Live BLE Mode and Simulator Mode</h3>
<p>Open the app &rarr; Navigate to <strong>Devices Screen</strong> (<code>lib/features/devices/device_screen.dart</code>).
Toggle the <strong>Live Hardware Mode</strong> switch. The app switches from <code>MockSensorDataSource</code> to <code>BluetoothSensorDataSource</code> and starts scanning for your ESP32.</p>

<h2 class="pb">4. Ready-to-Flash ESP32 Firmware (Arduino C++)</h2>
<p>Flash this sketch using the Arduino IDE with the <strong>ArduinoJson</strong> library installed:</p>

<pre><code>#include &lt;BLEDevice.h&gt;
#include &lt;BLEServer.h&gt;
#include &lt;BLEUtils.h&gt;
#include &lt;BLE2902.h&gt;
#include &lt;ArduinoJson.h&gt;

// UUIDs matching ble_constants.dart
#define SERVICE_UUID        "4fafc201-1fb5-459e-8fcc-c5c9c331914b"
#define CHARACTERISTIC_UUID "beb5483e-36e1-4688-b7f5-ea07361b26a8"
#define DEVICE_NAME         "PRANA_BAND_PRO"

BLEServer* pServer = NULL;
BLECharacteristic* pTelemetryCharacteristic = NULL;
bool deviceConnected = false;

class MyServerCallbacks: public BLEServerCallbacks {
    void onConnect(BLEServer* pServer) {
      deviceConnected = true;
      Serial.println("PRANA App Connected via BLE!");
    }
    void onDisconnect(BLEServer* pServer) {
      deviceConnected = false;
      Serial.println("App Disconnected! Restarting Advertising...");
      BLEDevice::startAdvertising();
    }
};

void setup() {
  Serial.begin(115200);

  // Initialize BLE Server
  BLEDevice::init(DEVICE_NAME);
  pServer = BLEDevice::createServer();
  pServer-&gt;setCallbacks(new MyServerCallbacks());

  // Create GATT Service &amp; Characteristic
  BLEService *pService = pServer-&gt;createService(SERVICE_UUID);
  pTelemetryCharacteristic = pService-&gt;createCharacteristic(
                      CHARACTERISTIC_UUID,
                      BLECharacteristic::PROPERTY_READ   |
                      BLECharacteristic::PROPERTY_NOTIFY
                    );
  pTelemetryCharacteristic-&gt;addDescriptor(new BLE2902());

  pService-&gt;start();
  BLEAdvertising *pAdvertising = BLEDevice::getAdvertising();
  pAdvertising-&gt;addServiceUUID(SERVICE_UUID);
  pAdvertising-&gt;setScanResponse(true);
  BLEDevice::startAdvertising();

  Serial.println("ESP32 BLE Advertising as: " DEVICE_NAME);
}

void loop() {
  if (deviceConnected) {
    // 1. Read your physical sensors (MAX30102, MPU6050, DHT22)
    float hr = 76.0 + random(-2, 3);
    float spo2 = 98.2 + (random(0, 10) / 10.0);
    float temp = 36.7;
    int steps = 3420;
    int battery = 88;

    // 2. Build JSON telemetry payload
    StaticJsonDocument&lt;256&gt; doc;
    doc["heartRate"] = hr;
    doc["spo2"] = spo2;
    doc["temperature"] = temp;
    doc["activityLevel"] = "Moderate";
    doc["steps"] = steps;
    doc["accX"] = 0.02;
    doc["accY"] = 0.04;
    doc["accZ"] = 0.98;
    doc["battery"] = battery;

    char buffer[256];
    serializeJson(doc, buffer);

    // 3. Send over BLE Notify
    pTelemetryCharacteristic-&gt;setValue((uint8_t*)buffer, strlen(buffer));
    pTelemetryCharacteristic-&gt;notify();

    Serial.print("Sent Telemetry: ");
    Serial.println(buffer);
  }
  delay(1000); // 1-second transmission interval
}</code></pre>

<h2>5. Verification &amp; Troubleshooting Checklist</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Bluetooth &amp; GPS Location:</strong> Ensure both Bluetooth and Location are switched ON on your testing smartphone (Android requires location permission to discover BLE peripherals).</li>
  <li><strong>ESP32 Serial Monitor:</strong> Open Arduino Serial Monitor at 115200 baud to confirm the device starts advertising.</li>
  <li><strong>Pairing in App:</strong> Open the PRANA app &rarr; Devices Tab &rarr; Toggle off "Simulator Mode" &rarr; Tap "Scan for Devices" &rarr; Tap "Connect" on <code>PRANA_BAND_PRO</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Data Confirmation:</strong> The heart rate and SpO2 readings on the Home Dashboard will update in real time every second.</li>
</ol>

